# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# One application, two windows.  Everything an application with more
# than one window needs, held in one place: both windows are THERE and
# wearing their own names, each takes the keys typed into it and no
# others, each publishes its own menus, and closing one closes ONE --
# the other stands, and so does the application behind both.
#
# Nothing here is about the spike application: every claim is about the
# runtime carrying the window id it was already given.
wait 25
note the shell's own folder window opens over them; it is focused, so
note the runtime's own close gesture takes it and leaves the two behind
click-window trk_script
key w ctrl
wait 10
note two windows, not one window wearing the second name: a runtime
note that aliases them shows only the first title, and only one window
click-window TwoAlpha
wait 6
expect-title TwoAlpha
click-window TwoBeta
wait 6
expect-title TwoBeta
note keys reach the window that has them, and no other
key x
key x
key x
wait 10
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/beta 3
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/alpha 0
click-window TwoAlpha
wait 6
key x
wait 10
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/alpha 1
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/beta 3
note the runtime carries a WHEEL to the window UNDER it, the way it
note carries a key to the window that HAS it: each pane counts only
note its own, and the direction it was rolled -- this is the legacy
note auto-start lane, now isolated from the desktop as well
press 499 261 4
wait 10
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/alpha wheel -3
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/beta wheel 0
press 757 261 5
wait 10
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/beta wheel 3
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/alpha wheel -3
note and the DESK's clipboard is one clipboard: what Alpha put on it,
note Beta reads back through the shared clipboard service
click-window TwoAlpha
wait 6
key y
wait 6
click-window TwoBeta
wait 6
key p
wait 10
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/beta clip from-alpha
click-window TwoAlpha
wait 6
note the strip carries the menus of whichever window is in front
click 60 8
wait 6
expect-menu Alpha typed 1
note the count row does nothing; taking it is how the strip is put
note away again without another gesture standing in for a click
menu-pick Alpha typed 1
wait 6
click-window TwoBeta
wait 8
expect-title TwoBeta
click 60 8
wait 8
expect-menu Beta typed 3
menu-pick Beta typed 3
wait 6
note an application can reach its OWN other window: the row is
note picked in the window in front, and the OTHER one comes forward --
note which is what a Window menu is, in the smallest form there is
click 60 8
wait 8
menu-pick Show the other one
wait 20
expect-title TwoAlpha
note and back, by hand, so what follows is asked of the window it was
note always asked of
click-window TwoBeta
wait 8
expect-title TwoBeta
note closing one window closes one window
key w ctrl
wait 12
expect-no-title TwoBeta
click-window TwoAlpha
wait 6
expect-title TwoAlpha
note and the application behind it is alive: it still takes keys
key x
wait 10
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_twowin/alpha 2
note the last window closing is the application ending
key w ctrl
wait 12
expect-no-title TwoAlpha
